OKLO won that informal comparison for three main reasons.

First, market-cap headroom. I compared its roughly $7B scale with something like RKLB around $46B. A 5× outcome requires very different terminal valuations:

7B\times5=35B

versus

46B\times5=230B.

That’s not sufficient to prove OKLO is better, but it makes the magnitude of the required commercial outcome less extreme.

Second was discrete de-risking. Advanced nuclear has a sequence something like:

\text{technical feasibility}
