\rightarrow
\text{financing}
\rightarrow
\text{construction}
\rightarrow
\text{commercial operation}

If the market currently assigns substantial probability to failure at each step, successfully crossing one can cause a nonlinear valuation change. That matched the Probability Collapse pattern we’d just extracted.

Third was a broader causal thesis we’d already been developing:

AI
\rightarrow
\text{datacenters}
\rightarrow
\text{electricity demand}
\rightarrow
