Even better: make two Grenade rankings

This is the distinction my first answer lacked.

Maximum Explosion

Optimize approximately for:

P(5\times)\times5\times\text{payoff}

We knowingly accept brutal failure rates.

Best Asymmetric Bet

Optimize for:

\frac{\text{probability-weighted upside}}
{\text{probability-weighted permanent capital loss}}

Those aren’t necessarily the same stock.

OKLO might rank #1 in Maximum Explosion while RKLB could potentially beat it in Best Asymmetric Bet because more of the business is already operationally demonstrated.

That’s much more useful.

